    "value": "Here are several GitHub resources and issues involving the usage of **WebTestClient** with Spring Boot:\n\n1. **Sample Project:**  \n   - [callicoder/spring-webclient-webtestclient-demo](https://github.com/callicoder/spring-webclient-webtestclient-demo)  \n   A sample showing how to consume and test REST APIs using Spring 5's Reactive **WebClient** and **WebTestClient**. Detailed steps and links to a tutorial are provided in the README【3:0†source】.\n\n2. **Common Issues:**  \n   - There are reports of exceptions if you use `@AutoConfigureWebTestClient` without the required web environment. For example, with `@SpringBootTest`, you need to specify `webEnvironment = WebEnvironment.RANDOM_PORT` or similar for WebTestClient injection to work correctly【3:2†source】.\n   - There is also a common pitfall regarding missing **WebClient** dependency in the classpath, leading to errors when upgrading Spring Boot versions. Fixes and discussions are found in related issues【3:8†source】.\n\n3. **Customization:**  \n   - Discussion on customizing **WebTestClient** in integration tests, example code, and challenges around URI builder configuration can be found [here](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/issues/15132)【3:5†source】.\n\n4. **Testing Infrastructure:**  \n   - There are enhancements and discussions about using **WebTestClient** for both Spring MVC (using MockMvc) and WebFlux and how this support has evolved【3:6†source】.\n\n5. **Spring REST Docs Integration:**  \n   - For integration with Spring REST Docs, see [this discussion](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-restdocs/issues/741) for examples and how to use REST Docs with **WebTestClient** in a Spring Boot environment【3:7†source】.\n\nIf you want to browse the source code for a module named `spring-boot-webtestclient`, it appears in the [spring-projects/spring-boot repository](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot), indicating there is now likely specific support for **WebTestClient** in Spring Boot. Look inside the `spring-boot-webtestclient` directory for further investigation【3:9†source】.",
