    "value": "The `spring-boot-webtestclient` module exists in both Spring Boot 3.4 and 3.5 releases. Here’s a summary regarding its presence and status in those versions:\n\n### Versions Available:\n- **Spring Boot 3.4.x**: The module `spring-boot-webtestclient` is part of this release series. However, as of June 2026, Spring Boot 3.4 has reached End of Life (EOL) for open-source support, but still receives enterprise support until the end of 2026【3:6†source】.\n- **Spring Boot 3.5.x**: The `spring-boot-webtestclient` continues to be supported in this version and is currently actively supported in OS and enterprise tiers. The latest release in the 3.5 series (as of June 2026) is 3.5.16, released on June 25, 2026【3:6†source】.\n\n### How to Use\n- The artifact you are likely looking for:\n  ```\n  \u003cdependency\u003e\n      \u003cgroupId\u003eorg.springframework.boot\u003c/groupId\u003e\n      \u003cartifactId\u003espring-boot-webtestclient\u003c/artifactId\u003e\n      \u003cversion\u003e3.5.x\u003c/version\u003e \u003c!-- or 3.4.x if using 3.4 series --\u003e\n      \u003cscope\u003etest\u003c/scope\u003e\n  \u003c/dependency\u003e\n  ```\n- In Spring Boot 4.x, note that you must explicitly add this module, as it’s no longer transitively included by `spring-boot-starter-test`【3:7†source】【3:9†source】.\n\n### Release Notes\n- For more information on what's new or changed in each minor version:\n  - [Spring Boot 3.4 release notes on GitHub](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/wiki/Spring-Boot-3.4-Release-Notes)\n  - [Spring Boot 3.5 release notes on GitHub](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot/wiki/Spring-Boot-3.5-Release-Notes)\n\nIf you need precise artifact version numbers, the pattern is typically `3.4.0`, `3.4.1`, ..., `3.5.0`, `3.5.1`, ..., etc., for the available patch releases【3:6†source】. \n\nLet me know if you need a complete list of all available patch versions for either 3.4 or 3.5!",
