    "value": "Here are some references to \"spring-boot-webtestclient\" in the context of the official Spring Boot GitHub repository:\n\n1. There was a regression issue in Spring Boot 4.0.0-M1 regarding WebTestClient being bound to the previous test server port when the application context is paused and restarted, affecting integration tests that use the fluent API. The issue was fixed for milestone 4.0.0-M2. If you're using WebTestClient for Spring MVC-based tests, you may want to review this thread for details and workarounds if you encounter such a problem【3:0†source】.\n\n2. The `@AutoConfigureWebTestClient` annotation and integration with WebTestClient only work if your test uses a web environment. If you use `@SpringBootTest` without specifying a web environment, WebTestClient will not be available for autowiring, leading to an exception. This is expected behavior, though some discussion suggests that the error message could be more clear. Ensure your test uses a web environment such as `WebEnvironment.RANDOM_PORT` when using WebTestClient【3:2†source】.\n\n3. For those who want to customize security configuration applied to WebTestClient, starting from Spring Boot 2.1.0, security can be applied via WebTestClientBuilderCustomizer. There are discussions and enhancements around adding a secure flag, similar to `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, to `@WebFluxTest` and `@AutoConfigureWebTestClient` for better integration with Spring Security【3:3†source】.\n\nIf you want to see the source and configuration files related to this, you can visit [the spring-boot repository](https://github.com/spring-projects/spring-boot) and look in modules like `spring-boot-webmvc`, but for direct references or issues, the above issues and discussions are your best starting points.",
